      ":question/worked-solution": "Collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)-2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\\\&=2\\left(\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x-\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\left(\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\right)&=2\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
